<title>CANADA: Propane leak as Canadian National derails.</title>
<headline>Propane leak as Canadian National derails.</headline>
<dateline>WABOWDEN, Manitoba 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Canadian National Railway Co propane tanker derailed near this northern Manitoba town and forced the temporary closure of a highway, the Royal Canadian Mounted Police said on Monday.</p>
<p>A propane tanker was leaking gas and forced the closure of Highway 6 which links Thompson to Flin Flon following the 1350 EST derailment, the RCMP said.</p>
<p>No one was injured and the derailment was still under investigation, the RCMP said.</p>
<p>Inco Ltd has a mine in Thompson and CN's Bay Line is the only link to Canada's northern grain port of Churchill.</p>
<p>(Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548)</p>
